# The 20-term vocabulary you need

If you remember nothing else, remember these.

<div class="cols three">
<div class="card">

**Carrier** — the insurance company
**Brokerage** — the agency
**Producer** — the salesperson
**Customer** — the policyholder
**MGA / GA** — wholesale layer
**Direct billing** — carrier collects
**Agency billing** — brokerage collects

</div>
<div class="card">

**Commission** — paid by carrier to brokerage
**Compensation** — paid by brokerage to producer
**Override / Carry** — carrier bonus to GA
**Producer Comp Plan (PCP)** — standing agreement
**Split (SIF)** — per-policy allocation
**Book of Business** — producer's portable asset
**Renewal vs. New** — different commission %

</div>
<div class="card">

**Point-in-time recognition** — earned at binding
**Fiduciary account** — segregated cash
**COBRA** — continuation cost; nets against comp
**Net vs. Gross** — before/after deductions
**Captive vs. Independent** — single carrier vs. many
**Statement** — monthly/quarterly carrier report
**Provider** — synonym for carrier

</div>
</div>

*Quiz yourself before any customer meeting.*

