# What this means for HSO

Three implications for HSO's go-to-market.

<div class="cols two">
<div class="card">

### **A real industry, not a feature**
Brokerage finance is a category, not a use case. Unite addresses it directly — no other product is purpose-built for this.

</div>
<div class="card">

### **A buyer with budget pressure**
Brokerages are PE-backed, growing through M&amp;A, hitting back-office walls. They have budget to spend on the bottleneck.

</div>
</div>

<div class="cols two">
<div class="card">

### **A pain that doesn't go away**
200 carriers × infinitely different statement formats. New carriers added every year. The mapping-studio AI capability *gets more valuable over time*, not less.

</div>
<div class="card">

### **HSO sells next to D365 — naturally**
Unite integrates with D365 Finance. Where HSO sells D365 today, Unite is the insurance-specific layer that adds vertical credibility.

</div>
</div>

